# Figma-to-React Native Pipeline

When given a Figma URL and asked to implement screens/flows, follow this complete pipeline sequentially.

## Phase 1: Analyze the design

Use `@figma` tools to understand the design:

1. `get_figma_file` — understand page/frame hierarchy
2. `get_figma_styles` — extract design tokens (colors, typography, spacing)
3. `get_figma_node` — get specific screen details (layout, children, constraints)
4. Identify: all screens, reusable components, navigation relationships

**Output before proceeding:**
- List of screens with descriptions
- List of shared components
- Navigation graph (screen A → action → screen B)
- Design tokens (colors, fonts, spacing)

## Phase 2: Plan

Before writing code, produce a brief plan:
- Theme files needed
- Components to build (in dependency order)
- Screens to implement (in navigation order)
- Test strategy (which flows to cover with Maestro)

**Ask for approval before proceeding.**

## Phase 3: Implement

Execute in this order:

### 3a. Theme (from Figma tokens)

```text
src/theme/
├── colors.ts        ← from get_figma_styles color fills
├── typography.ts    ← from get_figma_styles text styles
├── spacing.ts       ← from auto-layout padding/gap values
└── index.ts         ← re-exports + useTheme hook
```

### 3b. Shared components

- One file per component: `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx`
- Use theme constants (never hardcode colors/spacing)
- Add `testID` to all interactive elements
- Type all props with interfaces
- Use `StyleSheet.create()` for styles

### 3c. Screens

- `src/screens/<ScreenName>.tsx`
- Compose from shared components
- Add `testID` to screen root and key assertable elements
- Handle loading/error/empty states

### 3d. Navigation

- `src/navigation/` with typed navigators
- Define `RootStackParamList` with all route params
- Wire screens into navigators matching the Figma flow

## Phase 4: Tests

### Unit tests (Jest + React Testing Library)

```bash
# Run after implementation
npx jest
```

- Test component rendering with different props
- Test conditional rendering (loading, error, empty)
- Test user interactions (press handlers called)

### Maestro E2E flows

Generate `.maestro/flows/<flow-name>.yaml` for each user journey:

```yaml
appId: com.example.app
---
- launchApp
- assertVisible: "Screen Title"
- tapOn:
    id: "element-testID"
- assertVisible: "Next Screen"
```

Rules for Maestro flows:
- One flow per user journey
- Use testIDs (not text) for tapping
- Assert screen arrival after every navigation
- Include happy path + primary error case

## Phase 5: Verify

1. `npx tsc --noEmit` — type check passes
2. `npx eslint src/` — no lint errors
3. `npx jest` — tests pass
4. `maestro test --dry-run .maestro/flows/` — YAML valid (if maestro available)

## Phase 6: Ship

1. Stage all changes: `git add src/ .maestro/ __tests__/`
2. Commit: `git commit -m "feat: implement <flow-name> from Figma"`
3. Push: `git push`
4. Create PR with:
   - Figma link in description
   - List of screens implemented
   - Test coverage summary

## Figma → React Native mapping reference

| Figma | React Native |
|-------|-------------|
| Frame (vertical auto-layout) | `<View style={{ flexDirection: 'column' }}>` |
| Frame (horizontal auto-layout) | `<View style={{ flexDirection: 'row' }}>` |
| Auto-layout gap | `gap` or margins on children |
| Auto-layout padding | `padding*` properties |
| Fill container | `flex: 1` or `alignSelf: 'stretch'` |
| Hug contents | Intrinsic sizing (no flex) |
| Text node | `<Text style={typography.x}>` |
| Rectangle + fill | `backgroundColor` + `borderRadius` |
| Image fill | `<Image source={...}>` |
| Component instance | Reusable `<Component prop={...}>` |

## Rules

- Never hardcode colors/fonts/spacing — use theme
- Always add `testID` to interactive elements
- Always add `accessibilityLabel` to buttons and inputs
- One component per file
- `StyleSheet.create()` over inline styles
- Type all navigation params
- If Figma is ambiguous, ask — don't guess
